hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"78","It is narrated from Abu Abdullah al-Sanasaji that he performed the (Maghrib) prayer behind Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him). In the first two rak'ahs, he recited Surah Al-Fatihah and one short surah from the Mufassal with loud recitation. Then, when he stood up for the third rak'ah and began the recitation (al-Sanasaji says), I came so close to him that my clothes were touching his clothes. I heard him recite Umm al-Qur'an, and this verse: ""Our Lord, do not let our hearts deviate after You have guided us."" [آل عمران: 8]"
"79","Muhammad bin Wazir narrated to us the hadith, he said: Walid narrated to us from Abu Amr and Malik bin Anas, from Abu Ubaid, the companion of Ibn Suleiman, that Qais bin Harith narrated to Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, he heard it from Sanasaji, who narrates similar to the previous hadith. Abu Ubaid said: Ubadah bin Nasi informed me, he heard Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, saying to Qais bin Harith: How did you narrate the hadith to me from Sanasaji? He narrated this hadith to Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, so Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Since I heard this hadith from you before, I have not stopped acting upon it."
